.TH PACREACTD 1 "2026-11-20" "pacreactd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pacreactd \- watches the system and tells pacreact, pacbar and other programs what changed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacreactd
.br
.B pacreactd watch
.RI [ prefix ...]
.br
.B pacreactd get
.I key
.br
.B pacreactd print
.br
.B pacreactd \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments it runs as the daemon: it watches the battery and the charger, memory, CPU and I/O pressure, the temperature, the
network (and the wifi signal, from NetworkManager or iwd), the sound server and the audio jacks, the webcam, USB devices, printing (CUPS), the screen's brightness, disk space,
Bluetooth, the lock keys and, if asked, the latency of a host, and keeps what it knows as a table of keys and values. Programs
connect to its socket, are told the state, and then every change; it sleeps between them.
.PP
It has no screen and decides nothing about what is worth showing. The protocol, and every key, are in
.IR /usr/share/doc/pacreactd/protocol.md .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "watch [" prefix ...]
Print the state, then each change, one per line, until interrupted. With prefixes, only the keys under them (\fBnet\fR is
\fBnet\fR and \fBnet.*\fR).
.TP
.BI get " key"
Print the value of one key (its attributes, if any, after a tab). Exits 1 if there is no such key.
.TP
.B print
Print the print jobs that have not finished, one per line: id, state, queue and name. Asks CUPS when run; the daemon need not run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pac/pacreactd.conf, ~/.config/pac/pacreactd.conf, ./pacreactd.conf
Settings, each overriding the earlier. The example is documented and installed in
.IR /usr/share/doc/pacreactd/pacreactd.conf .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pacreactd.sock
The socket (a SOCK_SEQPACKET Unix socket, mode 0600).
.SH SYSTEMD
.B systemctl --user enable --now pacreactd.socket
starts the daemon when something first connects. Or enable
.B pacreactd.service
to run it with the session. Under systemd the socket exists before the daemon, and is not removed when it exits.
.SH SECURITY
Only processes of the same user may connect. What devices, documents and people call themselves is cleaned before it is
said, and can never be taken for anything but a name. See the protocol document.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacreact (1)
